"""Every code listing of the SEN0401 chapter 8 deck 2.0.0 (Digital Signatures; a NEW file, the deck 1.1.0 and its examples_v1_0_0.py stay unchanged) and the source of the chapter-code
manifest chapter_code_ch08_v1_0_0.json that the page's chapter-code tab reads. One entry per code slide, in SLIDE ORDER. A listing is a list of GROUPS; a group is a few single-line
statements and the plain-language note that explains them (the deck standard asks for an explanation beside every code box). Every statement is ONE line. The last row of a listing is an
expression (`final`, which is also in `show`): the slide prints its value under it, the only REPL text of the slide; the full result of the example is drawn as a chart or a table beside
the listing from the recorded `show` values (examples_run_v2_0_0.py), never typed. A statement is at most 56 characters, so that a code line never wraps (deck standard D12).
Every example uses only the chapter library of the page (the wheel with L = sen0401_ch07_script_lib, C = sen0401_ch08_sig_lib, K = sen0401_ch08_claims): none reads a saved evidence file, so each
runs in the browser as it runs here."""
__version__ = "2.0.0"

